"""PolicyLM launch entrypoint for the P7 GPU smoke, the throughput benchmark and (P8/P9) admitted runs.

``python -m dltrain.policylm_main bench --out-dir DIR --size S|M --width W --steps N`` builds a ``synthetic-scale/v1``
TrainData, a create-only run plan (``run_seed = os.urandom(32)``) and runs ``train.run`` on the plan's device with
local commits only, recording per-step wall time, CUDA memory and the CPU cost of draw+collate. It never writes S3.
The GPU path uses the deterministic CUDA mode of ``model.configure_determinism`` (CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG must be set
in the environment before CUDA initialisation).

``plan`` writes a run directory's create-only ``run-plan.json`` (+ ``data-spec.json``). ``run`` is one launch of
that plan (§5 P8 launch envelope, §6.8), inside a fixed ``jopedime-dltrain-*`` unit started by ``dltrain.launch``:

1. admission before CUDA initialisation (``gpu_gate.admission_probe``; REFUSE exits 3 and writes nothing else);
2. a create-only, self-declared launch receipt ``<run>/launch/<launch>.json`` (host, unit, INVOCATION_ID, pid,
   starttick, cwd, executable/argv sha256, run-plan sha256, admission sha256, source identities, GPU uuid);
3. data (the plan's refs must equal the data's), the store (none, the real create-only S3 store under
   ``research-only/models/policylm-v1/`` or its ``smoke/`` sub-prefix, or the guarded fake), the live producer
   (``<run>/launches/<launch>/live.json`` and ``<run>/live.json``, every <= 3 s; never ``claude/live.json``) and
   create-only update receipts under ``<run>/updates/``;
4. fresh, ``--resume`` (``train.resume_from_store``: §6.8 at-resume rules, CPU-only before any training step) or
   ``--resume-local``; before the first step the memory reserve is taken (free <= ceiling MiB) and the intake
   signals are re-checked; a watchdog thread runs ``continuation_probe`` at least every 15 s and the trainer checks
   its latest verdict before every optimizer step (YIELD/STOP/ABORT -> the §6.8 yield sequence; PAUSE blocks);
   the per-launch STOP file ``<run>/launches/<launch>/STOP`` yields too (never deleted; a resume is a new launch);
5. a create-only ``result.json`` per launch.
"""
